<BaseLayout title="About" description="Biographical context and computing philosophy.">
  <article>
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I am a software engineer and computer science practitioner with roots at the
      Silesian University of Technology (Faculty of Automatic Control, Electronics
      and Computer Science). My work focuses on exploring low-level operating system
      mechanisms.
    </p>

    <h2>Computing Environment</h2>
    <p>
      My primary thinking and editing environment is <strong>GNU Emacs</strong>
      alongside <strong>Org-mode</strong>. I operate exclusively on GNU/Linux
      systems, building terminal-centric workflows around C, Emacs Lisp, and Zsh.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read more about my bespoke configurations and open source utilities in the
      <a href="/projects">Projects</a> section.
    </p>

    <h2>Attributions</h2>
    <p>
      This site utilizes the <code>ef-autumn</code> palette created by Protesilaos Stavrou.
      Full license details and design inspirations are documented on the dedicated
      <a href="/credits">Credits page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
